  abstract = {Family is viewed as a hierarchically organized system, which is comprised of marital, parental and sibling subsystems.The interaction of family subsystems is important for understanding children's social development.Although numerous studies have indicated that marital and child-parent relationship are interrelated, it is unclear how marital relationship influences child-parent relationship.Researchers have argued that marital relationship},
